data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":463,"item_id":"fc_04de6b92baab60ea016adb442df6e0819188f034eef5ae6096","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"TASK_INCOMPLETE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"same-stage candidate 14; source closure and mathematical completeness still not achieved\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"I continued the R004 repair using the probed M011 bilinear Frechet integration-by-parts theorem, added N001 and N002 as direct inputs, and replaced the coordinate/Fubini argument with a compact-support product-integrability and derivative argument. I also added a direct M015 proof of zero integral in R001 and sources M013/M014/M016 for a planned compact-measure proof. Structural validation exposed remaining defects: earlier application mapping had to be corrected; the latest removal of old sources yields an input-reference error, and the ambient finite-on-compacts derivation is still only planned, not proved in R002. The M011 argument also still needs full mathematical audit and proof of its concrete integrability/support hypotheses. This is unfinished drafting/source closure, not a substantive gap.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Same-stage candidate 14 feedback: unknown graph input R001 after attempted removal of superseded old source nodes. Candidate 11 was structurally valid before later edits; M011 was successfully probed from recovered-library-source and used in the R004 patch. M015/M013/M014/M016 source probes are actual stage evidence. No submission or Audit A acceptance claimed.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"Started from base_candidate 11 and patched M011 proposition with its actual signature conditions; replaced R004 inputs with N001,N002,M001,M011 and rewrote argument to use direct time-window support and the general bilinear integration-by-parts formula. Replaced R004 applications with M001/M011 mappings. Candidate 12 surfaced an M001 mapping count error; candidate 13 surfaced obsolete source orphaning; candidate 14 attempted to remove M003/M007/M010 but checker returned unknown graph input R001. Need inspect and repair that exact candidate feedback, finish R002's proof that every compact Euclidean set has finite Lebesgue measure using the registered M013/M014/M016 and appropriate explicit quantifiers, establish Borel ambient facts/definitions, confirm M011 three integrability and derivative hypotheses in actual argument, finish local declarations and application checks, structural check, then submit complete graph.\\\"}\"}"}

